<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Conversation ability in text mode: the current exchange of one
  conversation. The communication (abilities/communication/communication.scx) invokes it
  as its child "conversation", routes each admitted input to it as
  bot.ability.conversation.routed_input {parent} (parent: the
  communication's input event as an envelope {event, data}), and records
  each spoken response with bot.ability.conversation.append. A direct
  bot.ability.conversation.input is taken too.

    inactive -input-> active { waiting -input-> running -> waiting }
    running { identifying_from -> identifying_memory? -> numbering_from?
              -> numbering_memory? -> tagging_memory? -> relating -> recalling_from -> recalling_memory?
              -> turn_exchange { readiness -> exchanging } (per source)
              -> remembering_from -> remembering_memory? -> committing }
    append, snapshot.request (any state)

  Relationships: each input
  first finds its relationship, {session_ref, context_ref, source_ids,
  target_ids, participants}, kept in relationships in the order
  they began. Input without targets shares the first relationship without
  targets (the ambient one). Other input takes the best scoring
  relationship, ties by session_ref: an ambient one whose participants
  include a target scores the similarity threshold (0.85); any other
  scores the lower of its source and target groups' match, in either
  direction (sources to sources and targets to targets, or swapped), the
  higher direction counting. Two groups match one to one, names equal and
  embeddings at least the threshold alike by cosine, refused when another
  assignment comes within the margin (0.05); the score is the
  mean. With no match the input begins a relationship of its own:
  context_ref is its relationship context reference
  ({"identity_groups":[...]}, the same in either direction), and session_ref "relationship-" and that. All of this is
  <conversation:relationship_for_input>. A source becomes a participant
  once its detector is ready (<conversation:participant_for_source>) and
  stops being one when its turn fails (<conversation:fail_turn>); a failed
  remember restores the participants the relationship had before the input,
  so a participant stays one while it has a detector.

  People (decisions D194 and D205): long-term memory holds people, each a
  stable participant ref person-<n> with the voice embeddings heard for
  them (bot_person, and bot_person_embedding of kind voice) and one
  representative voice (bot_person_centroid: its compact text, which the
  cognition's rest reinforces, abilities/consolidation/consolidation.scx).
  With a memory, an input with an embedding among its identities is
  identified before its relationship is found: identifying_memory asks
  the bot's memory (request "identify") for one read, every person's
  representative (oldest person first), and
  <conversation:people_for_input> matches each embedding by the
  relationships' match (cosine at 0.85, its margin 0.05, decision D90):
  the closest person, unless another comes within the margin, else a new
  person. When the input has new people, numbering_memory invokes it as
  "number" to take as many numbers from the people sequence (bot_sequence
  person, one upsert), and the input is matched again with the new people
  numbered on after the numbers taken before (the same match, so the same
  people), never from a count, so two bots on one database never number
  two people alike. The input in hand then holds each person's ref in its
  embedding's place, so its relationship, turns, participants, memory and
  committed message key on the person; tagging_memory then invokes it as
  "tag" to store the new people, every voice heard (each for its person,
  skipped when its person is no longer held: rest merged them meanwhile)
  and each new person's first voice as their representative, in one
  transaction. Each is bounded by memory_timeout_ms; a failure or timeout
  answers bot.ability.conversation.failed {stage: "memory", message} and
  commits nothing (numbers taken stay taken, as a sequence's do). Reading
  one compact row per person, identification holds about 100 people at
  256 dimensions: the memory ability's output event carries a result of
  about 43 KB and not one of about 47 KB (measured; a row is about 430
  bytes with its columns), and past it the identification times out at
  the memory stage. The namespace element's 64 KiB value bound (about 170
  people) and the sql service's 88 KiB result bound are above it.
  Without a memory there are no people: an embedding is its own
  participant (D79). Faces and the bot's own voice are not built.

  Memory (before and after the turns):
  with a memory (the <param> memory, the address of the bot's memory) it
  asks the bot's memory (abilities/memory/memory.scx, decision D265) as "recall",
  before the turns, with the relationship's memories (content where
  query_tags conversation_memory and context_ref is the relationship's
  context_ref, oldest first, at most 50), and as "remember", after them,
  with the input (kind conversation) as <memory:to_json> writes it: the
  JSON text {content, content_type, source_ids, target_ids} with sorted
  keys and compact separators, numbers as the data model's JSON numbers,
  the identities in identity order (names sorted, then embeddings by their
  JSON text) without repeats, and arrays and objects in the content tagged
  collision-safe (__stateforward_memory_content__ list, and mapping with
  its entries in code point order of their keys). The recalled
  memories are host-only (never in the output) and are
  logged by count only, once remembered. Each is bounded by
  memory_timeout_ms (5 s); a memory failure or timeout answers
  bot.ability.conversation.failed {stage: "memory", message} and commits
  nothing. Without a memory it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'">
  once per input.

  Turns: each input is one turn per source identity, in identity order
  (names sorted,
  then embeddings by their JSON; <identity:sorted_identities>), each exchanged with a turn detector
  (abilities/turn_detector/turn_detector.scx) invoked as "turn_detector"
  for that participant: its participant_ref is the participant's track
  (<conversation:new_track_ref>: the name itself, or for an embedding "track-" and its unit vector as
  JSON) and its conversation_ref the relationship's session_ref. Once it is ready
  (bot.ability.turn_detector.ready) the conversation sends it
  bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.start {conversation_ref, turn_ref,
  self_participant_ref, source_participant_ref, content} and
  bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.end; turn_ref is
  "input-<n>:turn:<track>", n counting this conversation's inputs. The
  content is <conversation:content_for_detector>'s: text/plain text as a text
  stimulus, audio/* content as an audio stimulus with its rate and
  channels, anything else as a content stimulus. Readiness and the turn
  are each bounded by turn_timeout_ms (5 s). A detector failure
  (bot.ability.turn_detector.failed), a timeout, or a turn the detector
  cannot take (an error.* here: a start its schema refuses) answers
  bot.ability.conversation.failed {stage: "turn_detector", message} and
  commits nothing. The turns' product is what is committed
  (<conversation:complete_turn>): the turns' texts joined by spaces as text/plain when
  any has text, each distinct text once (D79); else no content for audio;
  else the input's content. The committed provenance's turn_ref is the
  first turn's and its session_ref the relationship's; audio/* content is
  dropped (media never enters the model-facing exchange). Input that
  arrives while one is in hand is held by <event:defer/> (scxml.rs
  namespaces/event) and is taken, in order, on the return to waiting.

  Appends: outbound messages only, committed into the exchange with
  provenance event bot.ability.conversation.append. An append is already
  committed when its id (non-empty), source and target, which the message's
  provenance carries for the append event, match a message's in the current exchange; it is not committed
  again, and either way the conversation answers
  bot.ability.conversation.output.

  Snapshot: bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.request {request_ref}, in
  any state, answers bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.output
  {request_ref, detector_refs}: [session_ref, source] of every
  participant, ordered by relationship and then identity
  (<conversation:detector_refs>; floppy invokes a detector per turn, so a participant
  stands for its detector).

  Exchange (decision D176): an inbound commit opens a new exchange, [the
  inbound message], and its input becomes the exchange's parent; each
  outbound commit joins it; the next inbound replaces it. Nothing earlier
  is carried (what was said before is memory's). Every message carries
  participants (stamped by its producer and never inferred): an inbound
  one the participants <conversation:turn_participants> stamps for its
  turn (its string source_ids and target_ids, then whatever its parent's
  data carries), an outbound one those its producer stamped on the append
  (speaking stamps the bot's own voice once it has one, own true). A
  message's provenance, source_ids and target_ids are correlation, left
  out of what a model is shown (the cognition renderer drops them).
  An append is answered with the exchange's own parent, even while
  another input is in flight.

  Output: every commit's product is bot.ability.conversation.output
  {parent, messages}: the exchange, parent the input that opened it (an
  envelope {event, data}) and messages the exchange in causal order. An
  inbound commit of text (string content, content_type text/*) hands it to
  the parent as a stimulus, bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus,
  participants} (the product's envelope with source "conversation";
  participants the turn's); every other commit sends the product itself.

  Short-term memory (as mosfet.py's Conversation and Listening write
  it): every committed message with words is also written to the body's
  short-term register as a turn, bot.ability.memory.stm.turn {id,
  direction, speakers, text, cut, conversation} sent to the parent (the
  communication passes it to the body, which passes it to the register;
  a one-way message, so the commit never waits on it). An inbound text
  commit is a heard turn (speakers its turn's source participants), and
  speech reaches the conversation as its decoded words, so what the bot
  heard is written here whether it was typed or said; an outbound one is a
  said turn (speakers the participants its producer stamped, the bot's own
  voice). id is the message's provenance id, else its turn_ref, else the
  committing event's name; conversation is this session's id; the words
  are cut by <memory:cut_at_word>. A message whose content is not a
  string of a text/* type, or only white space, writes nothing. The
  register's turns are the body's, so a later turn in any relationship
  reads what was heard and said in every one.

  Readiness: the session's start sends bot.ability.ready to the parent
  (decision D242); it offers nothing (its input is not a tool event).

  Commits: <conversation:complete_turn> builds each inbound message and
  <conversation:message_for_turn> each outbound one; the document opens the exchange with an inbound one
  and appends an outbound one to it.

  Bindings: the bot, conversation, identity and memory namespace packages
  (the bot's memory, which the body invokes, binds the sql service).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:conversation="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/conversation"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:identity="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/identity"
       xmlns:memory="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/memory"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="conversation" initial="conversation">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The 5 s bound on each memory operation. -->
    <data id="memory_timeout_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <!-- Turns: the 5 s turn detector bound, the inputs taken so far,
         this input's sources in order, the one in hand, its track and the
         stimulus that opens its turn, the completed turns, and the turn
         timer. -->
    <data id="turn_timeout_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <data id="inputs" expr="0"/>
    <data id="turn_sources" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="turn_index" expr="0"/>
    <data id="track_ref" expr="null"/>
    <data id="turn_content" expr="null"/>
    <data id="turns" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The current exchange (decision D176): the inbound
         message that opened it, then the outbound ones committed since,
         and the input that opened it (its parent; null before one). -->
    <data id="exchange" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="exchange_parent" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Relationships, in the order they
         began: {session_ref, context_ref, source_ids, target_ids,
         participants}; the relationship in hand, its
         participants before this input, and the snapshot's detector references. -->
    <data id="relationships" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="relationship_index" expr="-1"/>
    <data id="participants" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="detector_refs" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The product's stimulus envelope, for the handoff. -->
    <data id="product" expr="null"/>
    <data id="parent" expr="null"/>
    <data id="input" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The participants the turn's cognition handoff stamps. -->
    <data id="turn_participants" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The message in hand, and its words as <memory:cut_at_word>
         bounds them for the short-term register. -->
    <data id="message" expr="null"/>
    <data id="words" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Memory: the address of the bot's memory (null: no memory) and its statements.
         The SQL runs on both
         engines (SQLite and Postgres). A memory id is the next row count
         as 32 zero-padded digits (neither engine's randomness is unique
         across invocations in Wasm); JSON rows are told by their
         content_format, the 50 most recent by created_at,
         then memory_id (the insertion order), read oldest first. The
         count recalled, for the log. -->
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D265). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="memory_select" expr="'SELECT content FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id FROM bot_memory WHERE query_tags = ?1 AND context_ref = ?2 ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC LIMIT 50) AS recent ORDER BY created_at, memory_id'"/>
    <data id="memory_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_memory (memory_id, scope, context_ref, subject_ref, kind, sensitivity, retention, content, content_format, query_tags) VALUES ((SELECT substr(\'00000000000000000000000000000000\', 1, 32 - length(n)) || n FROM (SELECT CAST(COUNT(*) + 1 AS TEXT) AS n FROM bot_memory) AS c), ?1, ?2, NULL, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7, ?8)'"/>
    <data id="recalled" expr="0"/>
    <!-- The input as <memory:to_json> writes it, to remember. -->
    <data id="memory_payload" expr="null"/>
    <!-- People (decisions D194 and D205): every person's representative
         voice, numbers taken from the people sequence, a new person, a
         voice heard for one (while they are held), a new person's
         representative; the representatives read, and what
         <conversation:people_for_input> made of the input. -->
    <data id="voice_select" expr="'SELECT person_id, centroid FROM bot_person_centroid WHERE kind = ?1 ORDER BY first_seq, person_id'"/>
    <data id="sequence_next" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_sequence (name, value) VALUES (?1, ?2) ON CONFLICT (name) DO UPDATE SET value = bot_sequence.value + excluded.value RETURNING value'"/>
    <data id="person_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_person (person_id) VALUES (?1)'"/>
    <data id="voice_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_person_embedding (person_id, kind, embedding) SELECT CAST(?1 AS TEXT), CAST(?2 AS TEXT), CAST(?3 AS TEXT) WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bot_person WHERE person_id = ?1)'"/>
    <data id="representative_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_person_centroid (person_id, kind, centroid, weight, first_seq, through_seq) SELECT CAST(?1 AS TEXT), CAST(?2 AS TEXT), CAST(?3 AS TEXT), 1, MIN(seq), MIN(seq) FROM bot_person_embedding WHERE person_id = ?1 AND kind = ?2'"/>
    <data id="held_voices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="people" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="conversation.js"/>

  <state id="conversation" initial="inactive">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
    </onentry>

    <state id="inactive">
      <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.routed_input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.routed_input.json"
                  target="running">
        <assign location="input" expr="_event.data.parent.data"/>
        <assign location="parent" expr="_event.data.parent"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.input.json"
                  target="running">
        <assign location="input" expr="_event.data"/>
        <assign location="parent" expr="inputEnvelope()"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <state id="active" initial="waiting">
      <state id="waiting">
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.routed_input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.routed_input.json"
                    target="running">
          <assign location="input" expr="_event.data.parent.data"/>
          <assign location="parent" expr="_event.data.parent"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.input.json"
                    target="running">
          <assign location="input" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="parent" expr="inputEnvelope()"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Identify the input's voices; then its relationship; recall
           its memories, exchange the turns, remember the input (nothing
           without a memory); then commit the turns' product. -->
      <state id="running" initial="identifying_from">
        <!-- Input that arrives meanwhile waits. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.routed_input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.routed_input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="conversation.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="conversation.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- Identify the people the input's voices are (decision D194). -->
        <state id="identifying_from">
          <transition cond="isUnidentified()" target="relating"/>
          <transition target="identifying_memory"/>
        </state>
        <state id="identifying_memory">
          <onentry>
            <send id="identify-after" event="identifying_memory.after" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
            <assign location="people" expr="null"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="identify-after"/>
          </onexit>
          <onentry>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.identify">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.identify"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="identifyStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('identify')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="numbering_from">
            <assign location="held_voices" expr="heardVoices(_event)"/>
            <conversation:people_for_input location="people" input="input" voices="held_voices" after="0"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('identify')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="memoryFailedMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="identifying_memory.after" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="'Conversation memory identification timed out.'"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <!-- New people take their numbers from the people sequence. -->
        <state id="numbering_from">
          <transition cond="hasNewPeople()" target="numbering_memory"/>
          <transition target="tagging_memory">
            <assign location="input" expr="people.input"/>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <state id="numbering_memory">
          <onentry>
            <send id="number-after" event="numbering_memory.after" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="number-after"/>
          </onexit>
          <onentry>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.number">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.number"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="numberStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('number')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="tagging_memory">
            <conversation:people_for_input location="people" input="input" voices="held_voices"
                                           after="numbersBefore(_event)"/>
            <assign location="input" expr="people.input"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('number')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="memoryFailedMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="numbering_memory.after" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="'Conversation memory numbering timed out.'"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="error.*" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="identifyErrorMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <!-- Store the new people, every voice heard, each for its person,
             and each new person's representative. -->
        <state id="tagging_memory">
          <onentry>
            <send id="tag-after" event="tagging_memory.after" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="tag-after"/>
          </onexit>
          <onentry>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.tag">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.tag"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="tagStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('tag')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="relating"/>
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('tag')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="memoryFailedMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="tagging_memory.after" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="'Conversation memory tagging timed out.'"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <!-- The people could not be made of the input (an error.* of
               the identification, taken before the tag starts). -->
          <transition event="error.*" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="identifyErrorMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <!-- The input's relationship and its turns' sources. -->
        <state id="relating">
          <onentry>
            <conversation:relationship_for_input location="relationships" indexlocation="relationship_index"
                                                 input="input"/>
            <assign location="participants" expr="relationship().participants"/>
            <assign location="inputs" expr="inputs + 1"/>
            <identity:sorted_identities location="turn_sources" ids="input.source_ids"/>
            <assign location="turn_index" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="turns" expr="[]"/>
          </onentry>
          <transition target="recalling_from"/>
        </state>
        <!-- Recall the relationship's memories, before the turns. -->
        <state id="recalling_from">
          <transition cond="isMemoryAbsent()" target="turn_exchange">
            <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
          </transition>
          <transition target="recalling_memory"/>
        </state>
        <state id="recalling_memory">
          <onentry>
            <send id="recall-after" event="recalling_memory.after" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="recall-after"/>
          </onexit>
          <onentry>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.recall">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.recall"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="memoryRecallStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="turn_exchange">
            <assign location="recalled" expr="recalledCount(_event)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="memoryFailedMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="recalling_memory.after" target="waiting">
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="'Conversation memory recall timed out.'"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <!-- One turn per source, each with its own detector. -->
        <state id="turn_exchange" initial="readiness">
          <!-- The source's track (null once every source has had its turn). -->
          <onentry>
            <conversation:new_track_ref location="track_ref" source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
          </onentry>
          <invoke id="turn_detector" type="scxml" src="../turn_detector/turn_detector.scx">
            <param name="participant_ref" expr="track_ref"/>
            <param name="conversation_ref" expr="relationshipRef()"/>
          </invoke>
          <state id="readiness">
            <onentry>
              <send idlocation="timer" event="readiness.after" delayexpr="turnDelay()"/>
            </onentry>
            <onexit>
              <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
            </onexit>
            <transition event="bot.ability.turn_detector.ready" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.turn_detector.ready.json" target="exchanging">
              <conversation:participant_for_source location="relationships[relationship_index]"
                                                   source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
              <conversation:content_for_detector location="turn_content" input="input"
                                                 source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
              <send event="bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.start" target="#_turn_detector">
                <content expr="turnStart()"/>
              </send>
              <send event="bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.end" target="#_turn_detector">
                <content expr="turnEnd()"/>
              </send>
            </transition>
            <transition event="readiness.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="waiting">
              <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
                <param name="stage" expr="'turn_detector'"/>
                <param name="message" expr="timedOutMessage('Turn detector readiness')"/>
              </send>
            </transition>
          </state>
          <state id="exchanging">
            <onentry>
              <send idlocation="timer" event="exchanging.after" delayexpr="turnDelay()"/>
            </onentry>
            <onexit>
              <cancel sendidexpr="timer"/>
            </onexit>
            <transition event="bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.complete"
                        event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.turn_detector.turn.complete.json"
                        cond="isExchangedTurn(_event)" target="turn_exchange">
              <assign location="turns" expr="turnsWith(_event)"/>
              <assign location="turn_index" expr="turn_index + 1"/>
            </transition>
            <transition event="exchanging.after" cond="isTimer(_event)" target="waiting">
              <conversation:fail_turn location="relationships[relationship_index]"
                                      source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
              <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
                <param name="stage" expr="'turn_detector'"/>
                <param name="message" expr="timedOutMessage('Turn detector turn')"/>
              </send>
            </transition>
          </state>
          <!-- Every source has its turn: on to memory. -->
          <transition cond="hasAllTurns()" target="remembering_from"/>
          <transition event="bot.ability.turn_detector.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.turn_detector.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <conversation:fail_turn location="relationships[relationship_index]"
                                    source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'turn_detector'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="error.*" target="waiting">
            <conversation:fail_turn location="relationships[relationship_index]"
                                    source="turn_sources[turn_index]"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'turn_detector'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="turnErrorMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <!-- Remember the input, after the turns. -->
        <state id="remembering_from">
          <transition cond="isMemoryAbsent()" target="committing"/>
          <transition target="remembering_memory"/>
        </state>
        <state id="remembering_memory">
          <onentry>
            <send id="remember-after" event="remembering_memory.after" delayexpr="memoryTimeoutDelay()"/>
            <memory:to_json location="memory_payload" message="input"/>
          </onentry>
          <onexit>
            <cancel sendid="remember-after"/>
          </onexit>
          <onentry>
            <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.remember">
              <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.remember"/>
              <param name="statements" expr="memoryInsertStatements()"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
          <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('remember')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="committing">
            <log label="conversation.memories" expr="memoriesLog(_event)"/>
          </transition>
          <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('remember')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
            <assign location="relationships[relationship_index].participants" expr="participants"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="memoryFailedMessage(_event)"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
          <transition event="remembering_memory.after" target="waiting">
            <assign location="relationships[relationship_index].participants" expr="participants"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stage" expr="'memory'"/>
              <param name="message" expr="'Conversation memory remember timed out.'"/>
            </send>
          </transition>
        </state>
        <state id="committing">
          <!-- The turns' product, committed in place of the input. -->
          <onentry>
            <conversation:turn_participants location="turn_participants" input="input" parent="parent"/>
            <conversation:complete_turn location="message" event="parent.event" input="input" turns="turns"
                                        session_ref="relationshipRef()" participants="turn_participants"/>
          </onentry>
          <!-- An inbound commit opens a new exchange; the one before it is
               not carried. -->
          <transition target="waiting">
            <assign location="exchange" expr="[message]"/>
            <assign location="exchange_parent" expr="parent"/>
            <log label="conversation" expr="inboundCommitLog()"/>
            <if cond="isTextMessage()">
              <!-- What the bot heard, remembered past this exchange. -->
              <if cond="hasWords()">
                <memory:cut_at_word location="words" words="message.content"/>
                <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" target="#_parent">
                  <content expr="heardTurn()"/>
                </send>
              </if>
              <assign location="product" expr="({})"/>
              <assign location="product.event" expr="'bot.ability.conversation.output'"/>
              <assign location="product.data" expr="({})"/>
              <assign location="product.data.parent" expr="parent"/>
              <assign location="product.data.messages" expr="exchange"/>
              <assign location="product.source" expr="'conversation'"/>
              <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
                <param name="stimulus" expr="product"/>
                <param name="participants" expr="turn_participants"/>
              </send>
            <else/>
              <send event="bot.ability.conversation.output" target="#_parent">
                <param name="parent" expr="parent"/>
                <param name="messages" expr="exchange"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </transition>
        </state>
      </state>
    </state>

    <!-- An outbound record, in either state, joins the exchange once;
         answered either way. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.append" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.append.json"
                cond="isOutboundAppend(_event)">
      <if cond="isCommittedAppend(_event)">
        <log label="conversation" expr="alreadyCommittedLog(_event)"/>
      <else/>
        <conversation:message_for_turn location="message" direction="outbound"
                                       event="_event.name" message="_event.data.message"
                                       provenance="_event.data.message.provenance"/>
        <assign location="exchange" expr="exchangeWithMessage()"/>
        <log label="conversation" expr="outboundCommitLog()"/>
        <!-- What the bot said, remembered past this exchange. -->
        <if cond="isTextMessage() &amp;&amp; hasWords()">
          <memory:cut_at_word location="words" words="message.content"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="saidTurn()"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </if>
      <send event="bot.ability.conversation.output" target="#_parent">
        <param name="parent" expr="exchange_parent"/>
        <param name="messages" expr="exchange"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- The participants' detectors, in any state. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.request" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.request.json">
      <conversation:detector_refs location="detector_refs" relationships="relationships"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.output" target="#_parent">
        <param name="request_ref" expr="_event.data.request_ref"/>
        <param name="detector_refs" expr="detector_refs"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.*">
      <log label="conversation.rejected" expr="rejectedLog(_event)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
